Built on the measurement the row's own notes demanded first (tracker
discussion + lab notebook 2026-09-19 12:15): on hypergumbo-core's 179 files
scip-python types 3,973 of the 4,133 method-call receivers the syntax arm
left module-less (96.1%; 3,840 stdlib, 96 in-repo, 37 third-party), where
the Rust arm measured zero; the two Python arms agree on kind 4,721 to 2.
The two shared-importer gaps that measurement exposed landed in PR #1082.

New optional package packages/hypergumbo-lang-scip-python (pipx extra
`scip-python`; the producer is `npm install -g @sourcegraph/scip-python
@0.6.6`), registering `scip_python`: backend scip, languages [python],
executes_analysed_code=False, merge anchor name-as-emitted over the
identifier token — the ast python analyzer's anchor (WI-kokiz) pairs with
it unchanged. gate / invoke / translate / analyzer mirror the rust-analyzer
package; failures travel as pass-silence codes (dependency_unavailable /
pass_crashed / unreported); a completed run that indexed nothing is a run.

The translation drops what the syntax arm never models (parameter symbols,
per-module __init__ declarations) and does the one thing the Rust arm never
did: an external callee keeps the receiver's MODULE, as a `calls` edge on
the syntax arm's own id shape (python:pathlib.Path:0-0:glob:unresolved with
a structured dst_ref and call_construct), so the two arms are comparable at
every call site and the I/O-boundary catalogue can read it.

ADR-0045's deferred wiring fires: this is the first non-executing backend,
so ruling 4's config tiers are consulted inside resolve_optin below the
environment. `[backends] scip_python = true|false` is accepted in either
tier for exactly the registry's config_optin_backends() — alternative arms
declaring executes_analysed_code=False — project replacing user, and still
refused as a trust key for the executing ones; both lists derive from one
declaration. `--backend scip-python` checks the wrapper and the binary
(exit 2 naming the install line otherwise) and writes HYPERGUMBO_SCIP_PYTHON;
`--backend tree-sitter` is an explicit OFF for every opt-in backend;
resolved_backend_set names both arms so the results cache keys a Python
two-arm run separately.

